WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:13.864
My mom keeps the ice pack in the freezer.

2
00:00:15.224 --> 00:00:19.465
She'd bought it for Tate when he sprained his ankle during basketball practice.

3
00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:23.366
I opened the freezer and got out the ice pack.

4
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:25.927
Then I put it on top of my head.

5
00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:28.348
It felt really good!

6
00:00:29.784 --> 00:00:32.786
"Don't melt my ice pack with your hot head, Iggy!"

7
00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:33.967
said Tate.

8
00:00:33.987 --> 00:00:37.249
"Can I try it?"

9
00:00:37.609 --> 00:00:38.489
asked Caswell.

10
00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:40.911
"Quiet, Caswell!"

11
00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:42.352
whispered Molly.

12
00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:44.353
"Iggy is thinking!"

13
00:00:44.373 --> 00:00:48.095
"Is your brain getting cooler?"

14
00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:50.157
asked Jenny hopefully.

15
00:00:50.177 --> 00:00:53.279
"Shh!" said Josh.

16
00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:55.340
"Let Iggy think!"

17
00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.303
"The ice pack is starting to work," I said after a moment.

18
00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:02.884
"I'm getting an idea."

19
00:01:04.645 --> 00:01:08.729
Josh, Jenny, Molly, and Caswell watched me, waiting to hear my idea.

20
00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:13.092
"It's not exactly an invention," I told them.

21
00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:16.235
"But it is a way for us to stay cool."

22
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:20.839
I put the ice pack back in the freezer.

23
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.621
Everyone was still looking at me.

24
00:01:23.641 --> 00:01:26.083
"We can go to the movies!"

25
00:01:26.603 --> 00:01:27.004
I said.

26
00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:32.218
"The movie theater is air-conditioned, and we will stay nice and cool there."

27
00:01:33.379 --> 00:01:34.980
Josh looked disappointed.

28
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.022
"I don't think my dad will let us go to the movies again.

29
00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:41.144
We just went to see a movie last week."

30
00:01:41.164 --> 00:01:45.306
"Movies cost a lot," said Jenny.

31
00:01:45.326 --> 00:01:48.528
"And the snacks cost even more!"

32
00:01:49.048 --> 00:01:49.889
added Molly.

33
00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.090
I held up my hand.

34
00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.952
"Just a minute," I said.

35
00:01:56.004 --> 00:01:58.266
"I told you only part of my idea.

36
00:01:58.707 --> 00:02:01.649
I thought of a way for us to earn money for the movie too.

37
00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:06.914
We can ask people in our apartment building if they need help doing chores."

38
00:02:08.195 --> 00:02:09.597
Jenny's face brightened.

39
00:02:09.617 --> 00:02:14.661
"Everyone is so hot, they'll be glad to have our help!"

40
00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:23.444
"You'd better ask Mom if it's okay to knock on our neighbors' doors," said Tate.

41
00:02:23.464 --> 00:02:25.805
Just at that moment, my mom came through the door.

42
00:02:26.945 --> 00:02:28.746
She was pulling her shopping cart.

43
00:02:28.766 --> 00:02:32.368
"Whew!" she said.

44
00:02:32.388 --> 00:02:34.288
"It's really hot out there!"

45
00:02:35.009 --> 00:02:36.509
She looked at the dark apartment.

46
00:02:36.529 --> 00:02:40.991
"And I guess the power still hasn't come back on."

47
00:02:41.011 --> 00:02:44.232
"Nope," said Josh.

48
00:02:44.252 --> 00:02:47.674
"But Iggy has thought of a way for us to stay cool!"

49
00:02:50.995 --> 00:02:52.776
I told my mom about my idea.

50
00:02:53.988 --> 00:02:58.412
She said it was great, as long as my friends got permission from their parents.

51
00:02:59.573 --> 00:03:02.015
And then she offered to take us to the movies later.

52
00:03:02.035 --> 00:03:06.439
"We can all stay cool together," she said.

53
00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:09.141
"Cool!" said Tate.

54
00:03:10.242 --> 00:03:18.549
We all laughed because Tate always says "cool" when he thinks something is really great.

55
00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.412
But this time Tate was right.

56
00:03:22.264 --> 00:03:24.325
Staying cool was cool!

57
00:03:25.906 --> 00:03:29.527
That afternoon we all worked together to earn money to go to the movies.

58
00:03:30.828 --> 00:03:32.909
We swept the front steps for Mr.

59
00:03:32.929 --> 00:03:37.091
Calabria. We took out four bags of junk for Mrs.

60
00:03:37.151 --> 00:03:39.432
Carroll. We took Dr.

61
00:03:39.492 --> 00:03:41.173
Stanley's dog for a walk.

62
00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:48.516
We scrubbed the kitchen floor for Molly and Caswell's mom.

63
00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:53.937
Then we sat down on the front steps outside to count our money.

64
00:03:53.957 --> 00:03:59.859
"We have 21 dollars and 45 cents," said Josh.

65
00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:04.220
"That's only enough for two of us to go to the movies!"

66
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.241
Molly said, disappointed.

67
00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:11.922
"And only enough to buy half a bag of popcorn," I added.

68
00:04:11.942 --> 00:04:17.264
"We could flip a coin to decide who can go to the movies," said Josh.

69
00:04:18.528 --> 00:04:20.869
"That's no fun," said Jenny.

70
00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:23.270
"We all worked hard today."

71
00:04:24.431 --> 00:04:25.311
Molly looked at me.

72
00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:30.653
"Maybe Iggy can think of how we can all go to the movies," she said.

73
00:04:30.673 --> 00:04:36.756
"Iggy had better put on his ice pack again," said Caswell.

74
00:04:38.036 --> 00:04:38.716
I nodded.

75
00:04:39.537 --> 00:04:41.758
Sweat was streaming down my face.

76
00:04:44.359 --> 00:04:46.980
We went upstairs to get the ice pack out of the freezer.

77
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.167
But do you know what we found when we got to my apartment?

78
00:04:53.451 --> 00:04:55.396
The ice pack was melting!
